1
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,610
Ah, Sinon!

2
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,300
You're late, Kitty. Kirito.

3
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,290
Who's there?

4
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:05,600
I've been out here so long.

5
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:06,940
I might catch cold.

6
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:10,590
Sugo!

7
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:12,980
You did a very bad thing, Kirito.

8
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:15,840
You know, I can still feel the pain.

9
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,340
It's over, Sugo.

10
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,460
You better turn yourself in.

11
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,860
You're finished.

12
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,310
Finished?

13
00:01:23,393 --> 00:01:24,223
Hardly.

14
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:27,778
There are lots of companies that
would kill to have me in my research.

15
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,097
And once it's complete there won't be
anything or anyone standing in my way,

16
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:35,377
then I'll be the god of this world.

17
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,640
Oh But first first I'm going to kill you.

18
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:48,800
Come on get up I said get up!

19
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:58,177
You think a piece of trash
like you can get in my way?

20
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,620
Did you think I'd let you slow me down?

21
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,760
Wanna know what the punishment is?

22
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,930
Death.

23
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,020
I won't accept anything less.

24
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:15,850
Damn.

25
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,797
My right eye's all foggy.

26
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,060
But I won't miss again, promise.

27
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,180
You bastard!

28
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,200
You little boy.

29
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,260
You're a piece of scum!

30
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:34,185
You don't have any real power!

31
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,380
And neither do you, Sugo.

32
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:43,000
I damn you!

33
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,730
No!

34
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,400
Such a weak weapon.

35
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:56,840
Too light.

36
00:02:57,180 --> 00:02:58,340
No reach.

37
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,880
And it's all I'm gonna need
to kill you once and for all.

38
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:22,400
Here your love, here's all we have.

39
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:30,320
Here, go away, here's all we own. Yeah,

40
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,460
yeah,

41
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:39,900
yeah.

42
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:11,230
Hurry up!

43
00:04:11,313 --> 00:04:12,474
She's waiting for you!

44
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,620
Asuna

45
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,340
Kirito

46
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,177
It's okay now.

47
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:00,160
It's over.

48
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:03,400
I fought the final boss just now.

49
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,188
And the last battle's over.

50
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,340
It's all over.

51
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,260
I'm sorry.

52
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:14,240
But I can't hear too well right now.

53
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,456
I think I know what you said, though.

54
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,920
What you meant.

55
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,460
That it's really over.

56
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:27,180
And finally, finally, I get to meet you.

57
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:38,380
So anyway, I'm Asuna, Asuna
Yuki, and I'm finally back.

58
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,980
I'm Kazuto Kirigaya.

59
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,520
Welcome home, Asuna.

60
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,820
Let's do it. Let's go.

61
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:27,880
I love you, I love you.

62
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,497
When I'm here,

63
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:04,920
I can't see the future I can't see?.

64
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:11,457
Even when I'm in the sky, I'm
still saying that I can't see.

65
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:16,097
I'm in the heart, I want to
say that I want to keep it.

66
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:21,680
I can't see the feeling that I can't see.

67
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:05,237
looking at this sentence could anyone
tell me how looks like that's all for?

68
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,977
today keep an eye out for
homework files 25 and 26

69
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:12,060
then make sure to upload
your answers by next week.

70
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,209
Thanks for waiting for me.

71
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,020
I'm tired.

72
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,660
Tired and hungry.

73
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:42,957
You're starting to sound
like an old man, Kirito.

74
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:47,569
Yeah, well, I feel like I've gotten
about five years older in the last month.

75
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:51,480
And by the way, it's
not Kirito, it's Kazuto.

76
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:52,960
This is real life.

77
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,497
You shouldn't call someone
by their avatar's name here.

78
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:58,140
Oh, sorry. I forgot. Oh, no.

79
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,397
Now what am I going to do?

80
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,857
Everyone will know it's me.

81
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:04,417
That's what you get for using
your real name for your avatar.

82
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,330
Eh,

83
00:09:05,413 --> 00:09:08,777
I guess it doesn't really matter because
everyone at our school is stuck in SAO,

84
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:09,690
same as us.

85
00:09:09,773 --> 00:09:11,484
My cover's probably blown, too.

86
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,499
Asuna, are you getting around okay?

87
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,817
I mean, is the rehab you're doing helping?

88
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:20,730
Mm-hmm.

89
00:09:20,813 --> 00:09:23,817
I finally got the okay to walk
around without my crutches.

90
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:27,660
Although, the doctors say I
shouldn't run just yet. You will.

91
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,440
By the way, Kirito... What?

92
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:36,140
Do you know that everyone
in the cafeteria can see us?

93
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:42,730
Seriously.

94
00:09:42,813 --> 00:09:45,166
That little oversight
is gonna cost you lunch.

95
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,800
Sorry, I didn't know.

96
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,340
I was wondering about
your dad. Is he okay?

97
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,137
He is, but he's still not
over this whole thing.

98
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:06,808
He quit as CEO and took
an early retirement.

99
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,817
And now that he's got all this free
time, he doesn't know what to do with it.

100
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:14,357
Hopefully dad can find a hobby
and maybe that'll cheer him up.

101
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:15,400
I hope so.

102
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:21,940
That night in the parking lot,
the police came and arrested Sugo.

103
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,920
Later, when they interrogated him,

104
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:30,812
he denied everything and tried
to pin the blame on Akihiko

105
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:32,410
Kayaba.

106
00:10:32,493 --> 00:10:36,982
But after the police questioned one of his
employees, Sugo confessed to everything.

107
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:40,080
As for those 300 SAO players,

108
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:44,017
when they came to, they couldn't
remember anything about the experiments.

109
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:48,557
The good thing is they didn't suffer any
neurological or psychiatric after-effects,

110
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,934
so everyone can go back to their lives.

111
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:54,140
But the fate of virtual
Miss was a different story.

112
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:58,461
This latest incident practically
destroyed the industry altogether.

113
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:03,380
In the end, wrecked
progress was dismantled.

114
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:06,480
Its parent company also
suffered a big hit.

115
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:08,997
Alo was shut down.

116
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,577
No surprise there.

117
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:15,097
And as for the five or six other
vr Miss With all the negative

118
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:18,533
press and the public outcry
Their days were numbered too?

119
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,657
You know who I was just thinking about?

120
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,799
The commander What happened to him?

121
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:25,970
Oh

122
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,550
Yeah

123
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:33,120
Kayaba's dead They say it
was suicide No way Yeah,

124
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:36,217
when the world of SAO
collapsed He did a high-output

125
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,657
scan on his brain and
fried it when it was over.

126
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:39,570
So, wait.

127
00:11:39,653 --> 00:11:42,757
Was he trying to copy his
consciousness to the net or something?

128
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:47,428
Well, it's one in a thousand shot for
it to work, but I know he pulled it off.

129
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,940
That day, Kayaba spoke to me.

130
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,140
Or his consciousness did, anyway.

131
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,710
What's this?

132
00:11:55,793 --> 00:11:57,525
The beginnings of a new world.

133
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,040
I call it the seed.

134
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:03,220
Once it sprouts, you'll know what it is.

135
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:05,797
What you do with it is up to you.

136
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,939
You can even delete it if you want.

137
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:09,370
However,

138
00:12:09,453 --> 00:12:12,997
if you still have a tiny bit of
fondness left for the virtual world,

139
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,433
you'll take care of it.

140
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:18,020
Kirito? Kirito?

141
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,177
Don't forget, we're
meeting the others later.

142
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,090
Huh?

143
00:12:21,173 --> 00:12:22,003
Oh yeah, right.

144
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:23,577
Sorry I was spacing out.

145
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,540
As always.

146
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,477
It doesn't matter whether
you're in the game or IRL.

147
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:30,442
The minute you relax, you
space out like a champ.

148
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:34,050
Hmph.

149
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:44,477
Seriously, Lika, you're driving
me crazy with all that slurping.

150
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,700
Leave me alone.

151
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,908
He's all over her, and
it's driving me nuts.

152
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,280
Acting like that at school, it's so tacky.

153
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:55,987
Spying on them's kind
of tacky too, you know.

154
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,410
Uh...

155
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,917
If I'd have known it
was gonna be like this,

156
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,317
I wouldn't have let you talk
me into a mop-pong truce.

157
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,977
I didn't talk you into
it, it was your idea!

158
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:08,477
You said we should let them have their
lil' romance for a month, remember?

159
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,520
I mean, God, talk about naive!

160
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:18,699
It's gonna be cool meeting
everyone today, isn't it?

161
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,060
Yeah, I can't wait!

162
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,620
Sugu, I forgot to ask before.

163
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,877
Did you ever meet Egil?

164
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,790
Yeah.

165
00:13:37,873 --> 00:13:40,237
We went hunting together
a couple of times in ALO.

166
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,040
His avatar is ginormous.

167
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,397
Yeah, well, get ready, because
he's that big in real life, too.

168
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,362
Prepare to have your mind blown.

169
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,080
Hold on a sec.

170
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,416
Were we supposed to get here earlier?

171
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:06,757
We gave you a later time to make
sure everyone else got here first.

172
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:10,077
It wouldn't be right for the guests of
honor to show up before all the guests.

173
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:12,037
Don't just stand there, come on in.

174
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,950
Uh, hey.

175
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:15,177
Okay, let's get this party started.

176
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,672
You all know what to do.

177
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,350
Ready, and...

178
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:21,760
Congratulations on beating SAO, Kittito!

179
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:27,830
Cheers!

180
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:29,370
Cheers!

181
00:14:29,453 --> 00:14:30,283
Cheers!

182
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:39,102
Bartender, bourbon on the rocks.

183
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:45,890
Whoa, dude.

184
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,157
This is Long tea.

185
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,070
Thank you.

186
00:14:48,153 --> 00:14:49,291
Slide me a big boy drink.

187
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,100
Klein, seriously?

188
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,894
Aren't you supposed to go back to work?

189
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,320
Alcohol makes the overtime go by faster.

190
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,310
Uh-oh.

191
00:15:00,393 --> 00:15:01,223
Chick alert.

192
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,760
Long time no see. Hi, Thinker.

193
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,299
How have you been?

194
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,929
I heard that you and
Yulia are married now.

195
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:11,380
I know it's late, but congrats.

196
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,310
Thank you.

197
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,657
But ever since we got back,

198
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:17,657
it's been taking everything
we've got to adjust to life here.

199
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:20,677
The good thing is, I'm
settling into work mode again.

200
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,737
Congratulations on getting that far.

201
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:25,837
Hey, I've been reading the
new MMO today. Nice job.

202
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,567
Yeah, I wish it were better.

203
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,880
It could have used a bit
more content. Oh, well.

204
00:15:31,220 --> 00:15:34,691
With the way Miss are now, who
needs walkthroughs and news?

205
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:37,077
Those things are going to
be irrelevant soon, anyway.

206
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:39,537
You know what they say about
how the universe was born.

207
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:40,914
First there was chaos.

208
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:44,420
By the way, Egil, has
the seed been doing okay?

209
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,220
It's doing amazing.

210
00:15:46,660 --> 00:15:49,040
We got 50 mirrors already set up.

211
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,600
It's been downloaded 100,000 times.

212
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,037
And check this out.

213
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:56,002
It's got 300 big-ass
servers actually running it.

214
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,380
After I visited Asuna at the hospital,

215
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:04,600
I took the thing Kayaba called the Seed
over to Egil and asked him to check it out.

216
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:09,317
Turned out it was a full-dive
MMO that Kayaba developed.

217
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:12,297
It came in a program package
called the World Seed,

218
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:17,027
a stripped-down version of the Cardinal
system that could run on small servers.

219
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:20,277
Kayaba had modified the
program so that anyone

220
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:23,066
with access to an ordinary
server could easily

221
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,417
download it and use it to create
their very own online world.

222
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:29,640
After Egiel said it was safe to use,

223
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,677
I had him upload it to servers across the

224
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,584
globe so that everyone
could access it for free.

225
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:42,477
It turned out that was exactly what virtual
Miss needed to keep the genre going.

226
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,040
As for Alfheim Online,

227
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:48,986
all the data was transferred to a new
company that decided to keep it online and

228
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,350
running.

229
00:16:51,433 --> 00:16:54,337
But the new Alfheim wasn't the
only world born out of the seed.

230
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:57,237
Everyone from individual
gamers to a few hundred small

231
00:16:57,320 --> 00:17:01,026
companies were suddenly creating
brand new worlds on their very

232
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,477
own virtual game servers.

233
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:05,777
The best part is they were
all connected to each other.

234
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:09,317
It's almost to The point where you
could create a character in one world,

235
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:12,097
then transfer it to another
with all its skills intact.

236
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:18,997
Hey, has anything changed for
tonight's after party? Nope.

237
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,500
we're still on for 11.

238
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,960
we're meeting up in Yggdrasil City

239
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:51,100
I don't know.

240
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:23,789
You know, I had a feeling you
were going to fly too high up.

241
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,276
It's almost 11, so I came to get you.

242
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:28,840
Oh, okay, thanks.

243
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,360
Hey, Kazut, er, Kirito?

244
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:38,137
You know how ALO's got a
new company running it now,

245
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:41,280
and how you can use your
old SAO avatar if you want.

246
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:46,580
Everyone else is using their old
avatar, so how come you're not? Hmm.

247
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:52,644
I guess because in that world,
that Kirito's mission is over now.

248
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:55,620
I guess so.

249
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:00,257
Then I was the first to
meet the Spriggan version

250
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:03,222
